ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":164,"area":165,"prev":167,"next":170,"titles":173,"firmware":62},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":27,"procedures":86,"parameters":128,"related":129,"body":137,"sources":138,"official_url":31,"controls":152},"howto.control-synth-midi","Recipe — play an external synth over MIDI",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"control a synth","sequence external synth","sequence a hardware synth","trs midi","din midi","midi out","external midi track","howto",20,"knowledge/manual/units/howto/control-synth-midi.md",{"modes":16,"screens":18},[17],"auxiliary",[],"Set the multi-out to midi before plugging in a TRS-to-DIN cable (USB gear needs no setting), then play and sequence the synth from `T3` in auxiliary mode on the synth's channel, set on `M1`. TE's steps set no project MIDI channel; set clock to both only if the synth should follow the tempo.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":25,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[24],"1.0.15","1.1.15",null,[28,33,37,40,43,47,50,53,58,64,67,71,74,78,82],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"din","Synths with DIN MIDI sockets need the multi-out set to midi and a type A TRS-to-DIN cable, DIN end into the synth, jack into the multi-out.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#how-to-control-a-synth-with-midi","official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":36,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"one-job","The multi-out does one job at a time, so in midi mode it carries no CV, gate, sync pulse or audio.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/hardware-overview#inputs-outputs",{"id":38,"text":39,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"usb","Synths with USB MIDI plug into the OP-XY's USB-C port (through an adapter if needed), need no multi-out setting and appear under `com → M3`.",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"devices-din","TE's how-tos point to the devices page (`com → M3`) only for USB gear; whether a synth on the multi-out appears there is not documented.",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":46,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"track","The external MIDI track is `T3` in auxiliary mode; its keyboard and sequencer play the connected synth.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#external-midi",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":46,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"channel","On the track's `M1` page, `E1` sets the MIDI channel — match the channel the synth listens on — while `E2` and `E3` pick bank and program.",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"no-project-channel","TE's steps set only that `M1` channel; the project's midi page (`project → M4`) is not part of them.",{"id":54,"text":55,"source":56,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":57},"no-project-community","Community tools also report that the external MIDI track and midi-engine tracks send without a project MIDI channel; not yet checked on a unit.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#81-normal-operation","community",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":61,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"notes-on","On a unit with stock settings, notes in the midi section of the system settings (`com → M1`) is at both, which includes sending.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133","1.1.33","verified",{"id":65,"text":66,"source":61,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"clock","Clock is its own switch in the same section; at the stock setting (in) `play` and `stop` send no start, stop or clock ticks, and set to both they send start and stop with a constant tick stream (seen over USB).",{"id":68,"text":69,"source":70,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":57},"clock-jack","Community tools report that clock, start and stop go out over TRS MIDI as well as USB under that switch; only USB has been checked on a unit.","https://github.com/jshph/opxy-reactive/blob/master/DESIGN.md",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"ccs","`M2` and `M3` hold eight CC slots: `shift` plus an encoder switches a slot on and picks its CC number, turning the encoder sends values, and the moves can be sequenced and recorded.",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":77,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"several-synths","To sequence several synths, instrument tracks can run the midi engine too; TE's guide still calls it \"external\", its name before OS 1.0.15.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.15",{"id":79,"text":80,"source":81,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"engine-1133","On OS 1.1.33 the preset browser listed no midi engine, so `T3` is the route to use on that firmware.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#26-preset-browser-shift--m1",{"id":83,"text":84,"source":85,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":57},"own-engine","To send the notes of a track on one of the OP-XY's own engines as well, community tools say to give it a channel on the project's midi page.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#23-transmit-routing",[87,99,112],{"id":88,"goal":89,"preconditions":90,"steps":92,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"connect","Point the external MIDI track at a synth",[91],"nothing is plugged into the multi-out yet",[93,96],{"keys":94,"note":95,"set":26},"com → turn E3","midi; then connect the cable",{"keys":97,"note":98,"set":26},"auxiliary → T3 → M1 → turn E1","the synth's MIDI channel",{"id":100,"goal":101,"preconditions":102,"steps":103,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"cc","Control a synth parameter by CC",[],[104,106,109],{"keys":105,"note":26,"set":26},"M2/M3",{"keys":107,"note":108,"set":26},"shift + turn E1…E4","switch the slot on, choose the 